<title>UK: Russia's Novorossiisk still shut due heavy swell.</title>
<headline>Russia's Novorossiisk still shut due heavy swell.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Black Sea ports of Novorossiisk and Odessa were shut on Tuesday due to bad weather while pipeline deliveries to the Baltic port of Ventspils have been shut off due to full tank capacity, shipping inspector Petrak said.</p>
<p>Novorossiisk has been closed since 2320 local time on Saturday due to heavy swells ranging 0.7 to 1.2 metres, Petrak said.</p>
<p>On Tuesday, two crude tankers were alongside waiting to load and another two were at anchor waiting to berth.</p>
<p>Petrak said pipeline deliveries to Ventspils in Latvia  had been shut off at 0355 local time on Tuesday after storage tanks reached full capacity.</p>
<p>Two crude tankers were reported to be alongside waiting to load, while another four crude tankers and eight gas oil tankers were at anchor waiting to berth.</p>
<p>-- Melanie Goodfellow, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7714</p>
</text>
